    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68b3ec94_593f7768",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/RfcommCapabilities.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T22:10:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that the same requirement exists for L2CAP COC, it might make sense to extract it as a common marker of socket capabilities.\n\nUltimately it represents the maximum size of PDUs handled by the offload stack right ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "dde33f2109c44206e2918231638781124aa520dd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9dad9454_a9c29374",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/RfcommCapabilities.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959878
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T23:06:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I think it is the equivalent of the MTU for L2CAP COC. The naming here is to follow the RFCOMM specs. Is the suggestion here to just rename or use the common structure for the L2CAP COC and RFCOMM capabilities? @jaydenk@google.com any thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "68b3ec94_593f7768",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "dde33f2109c44206e2918231638781124aa520dd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "febfe8bb_19e2023c",
        "filename": "bluetooth/socket/aidl/android/hardware/bluetooth/socket/RfcommCapabilities.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-23T00:30:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For RFCOMM frame, actually there are two layers - L2CAP and RFCOMM and each layer has own maximum cap like L2CAP\u0027s `MTU` and RFCOMM\u0027s `Maximum Frame Size`. I hope to specify the exact field name for this protocol.",
      "parentUuid": "9dad9454_a9c29374",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "dde33f2109c44206e2918231638781124aa520dd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a25e1427_cd84c012",
